// endpoint_bind_workspace_session.proto — BindWorkspaceSession. SIDEBAR
// section. Point a workspace at a DIFFERENT vendor conversation in its own
// directory, chosen from ListWorkspaceTranscripts.
//
// THE BINDING IS THE WORKSPACE'S, NOT THE SESSION'S. What changes is which
// conversation the workspace's session record names, so the choice survives a
// restart, a hibernation and a daemon handover exactly as the rest of that
// record does.
//
// IT IS A SESSION SWAP, AND IT IS SAID SO. The daemon ends the current
// session and starts one on the named conversation through the ORDINARY
// resume — so a cold conversation is REFUSED with its cost and answered at
// the cold gate, the same refusal a revival meets. Binding never pays for a
// cold read silently.
//
// TWO WRITERS ON ONE CONVERSATION IS DATA LOSS, so a transcript another
// process is driving, or another workspace already holds, is refused by name
// rather than merged.
//
// A BIND IS NOT AN INTERRUPT: it is refused while a turn is in flight, as
// every other session-level verb is.

